WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.311
ModFalk gives AI agents the context to act.

00:00:03.311 --> 00:00:11.175
It connects evidence, sources, and memory in Falkor DB, so each result comes with a path you can inspect.

00:00:11.175 --> 00:00:14.900
Let’s see how that works across four different domains.

00:00:15.306 --> 00:00:16.895
First, Case Evidence.

00:00:16.895 --> 00:00:21.662
Choose a case and jurisdiction, then run the agent.

00:00:21.662 --> 00:00:25.370
It connects events, witnesses, statements, and exhibits.

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:29.077
Here, two statements give different arrival times.

00:00:29.077 --> 00:00:36.492
The result identifies the conflict, links the passages, and proposes a lawyer review task.

00:00:36.492 --> 00:00:39.140
The cases are generated examples.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:45.496
Official legal guidance covers the United States, England and Wales, and Canada.

00:00:45.902 --> 00:00:47.436
Next, Medical Overlook.

00:00:47.436 --> 00:00:54.080
It connects medicines, conditions, and allergies to a public Daily Med drug label.

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:59.190
Running it reveals a contraindication supported by the label text.

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:04.301
You can inspect the source, connected path, and evidence gaps.

00:01:04.301 --> 00:01:06.856
These patient records are synthetic.

00:01:06.856 --> 00:01:09.922
The alert requires a clinician's review.

00:01:10.329 --> 00:01:15.910
Disaster Response uses National Weather Service alerts and FEMA shelter records.

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:22.507
Without verified connections to facilities, routes, and capacity, the agent returns needs evidence.

00:01:22.507 --> 00:01:28.089
That missing information stays visible, and no response action is created.

00:01:28.495 --> 00:01:32.130
Now, switch to a clearly labelled example scenario.

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:38.036
This demonstrates how facilities, roads, shelters, and capacity can form a response path.

00:01:38.036 --> 00:01:44.852
The shortest path query is visible here, together with the assumptions that still need checking.

00:01:44.852 --> 00:01:49.395
Any proposed incident brief remains in the human review queue.

00:01:49.801 --> 00:01:56.624
For Sports Forecast, select Argentina against France in the twenty twenty two World Cup final.

00:01:56.624 --> 00:02:03.447
Set the replay to thirty minutes, with Argentina leading one nil, and run the agent.

00:02:03.447 --> 00:02:11.179
It uses match history and the entered score to calculate home win, draw, and away win probabilities.

00:02:11.179 --> 00:02:17.092
The result includes its model version, holdout evaluation, source links, and lineup context.

00:02:17.092 --> 00:02:18.911
These probabilities are uncertain.

00:02:19.318 --> 00:02:21.905
The context also survives between runs.

00:02:21.905 --> 00:02:28.805
Earlier findings, citations, and tool calls are stored in Falkor DB and retrieved as graph memory.

00:02:28.805 --> 00:02:32.254
Below, proposed actions enter a persistent review queue.

00:02:32.254 --> 00:02:35.273
A person can review or dismiss them.

00:02:35.273 --> 00:02:43.898
You can also inspect the actual queries behind the result, tracing the evidence from the source to the proposed action.

00:02:44.304 --> 00:02:50.311
That’s ModFalk: connected data, persistent memory, and decisions you can trace.

00:02:50.311 --> 00:02:53.587
Four agents, with one shared approach.

00:02:53.587 --> 00:02:55.225
Follow the source.

00:02:55.225 --> 00:02:56.863
Show the path.

00:02:56.863 --> 00:02:59.594
Keep the human in control.
